# Go workspace files: they change local builds silently and are ignored by
# `go install pkg@latest` anyway.
go.work
go.work.sum

# `make build` puts every binary here, so one line covers all of them and a new
# command needs no edit — the same "discovered, not maintained by hand" rule the
# Makefile follows for the module list.
/bin/

# A safety net for building by hand inside a module (`cd ai-sum && go build .`),
# which drops the binary next to the source. Only the Windows spelling can be
# matched generically; an extensionless one shows up in `git status`.
*.exe

# Coverage artifacts, written per module by `make cover`.
coverdata/

.DS_Store
